      "message": "Q:why do we need a version 2?\nA:Because of cost our HW removes redundant logic \u0026 register. And HW also reorganizes register map, this is more intuitive and easier to use for firmware. \n\nQ:Is this just the driver for version it83201 and the existing driver is for it8320?\nA:The existing driver is for it8320. Driver v2 is for new chip ex.it8xxx1 or it8xxx2 later series. \n\nQ:How different are they, the tcpc driver something we can share between them? We should pull out as much common code as we can between the two drivers. \nA:No, HW removes, adds, and reorganizes registers, so the new chips should use the new driver.\n\nQ:This one should be called tcpm_it8320XX.c as well. V2 doesn\u0027t tell us enough about what the driver is used for.\nA:Ok, but V2.c is already in tcpm folder, shall we still call it \"tcpm_ \" in name?",
